BLST's C server already defines and initializes __blst_platform_cap.
Reference that storage from Mach-O assembly instead of declaring an
additional COMMON symbol. GHC 9.14's runtime linker rejects the strong
C definition followed by COMMON as incompatible sizes (0 versus 4)
when loading simplexmq for Template Haskell.

Only symbol linkage changes; CPU detection and cryptographic operations
remain in the existing BLST implementation.

